(defrule dual-memory -> dual-memory-tension dual-memory-episodic dual-memory-working dual-memory-combined dual-memory-design-evolution)
(defrule dual-memory-tension -> :nucleus dual-memory-tension/n :elaboration-additional dual-memory-tension/a1 :elaboration-additional dual-memory-tension/a2 :elaboration-additional dual-memory-tension/a3)
(defrule dual-memory-tension/n -> :instruction "考える段階が履歴を必要とする一方で、全履歴を渡せない矛盾を 1 文で書く" :sample "The thinking phase (Phase 1 of the ReAct loop, Section 2.2.6) requires conversation context for strategic reasoning, but the full conversation history can grow to hundreds of thousands of tokens.")
(defrule dual-memory-tension/a1 -> :instruction "履歴を全部渡せない理由を 1 文で書く" :sample "Providing the thinking model with unbounded history is infeasible: it would exceed the model’s context window and waste budget on stale detail.")
(defrule dual-memory-tension/a2 -> :instruction "直近だけを渡す場合の問題を 1 文で書く" :sample "Providing only recent messages loses strategic context, causing the agent to “forget” its overall goals.")
(defrule dual-memory-tension/a3 -> :instruction "解決の着想を 1 文で書く" :sample "We resolve this tension through a dual-memory architecture inspired by human cognitive science, which separates compressed long-range context from detailed short-range context.")
(defrule dual-memory-episodic -> :nucleus dual-memory-episodic/n :elaboration-additional dual-memory-episodic/a1 :elaboration-additional dual-memory-episodic/a2 :elaboration-additional dual-memory-episodic/a3)
(defrule dual-memory-episodic/n -> :instruction "全履歴の要約が担う長い範囲の文脈を 1 文で書く" :sample "An LLM-generated summary of the full conversation history captures strategic, long-range context: decisions already made, overall goals, key findings, and important file paths.")
(defrule dual-memory-episodic/a1 -> :instruction "要約で残す情報の指示を 1 文で書く" :sample "The summarizer is instructed to preserve actionable identifiers (file paths, function names, variable names, error codes) while omitting verbose tool outputs and redundant exchanges.")
(defrule dual-memory-episodic/a2 -> :instruction "要約を作り直す頻度を 1 文で書く" :sample "This summary is regenerated periodically (every 5 new messages, controlled by a regenerate_threshold parameter) rather than on every turn.")
(defrule dual-memory-episodic/a3 -> :instruction "作り直す利点を 1 文で書く" :sample "By regenerating from the full history, each episodic memory snapshot is a fresh compression rather than a compression of a compression.")
(defrule dual-memory-working -> :nucleus dual-memory-working/n :elaboration-additional dual-memory-working/a1 :elaboration-additional dual-memory-working/a2)
(defrule dual-memory-working/n -> :instruction "直近の往復をそのまま残すことを 1 文で書く" :sample "The last several message pairs (the most recent 6 exchanges by default, controlled by exclude_last_n) are reproduced verbatim.")
(defrule dual-memory-working/a1 -> :instruction "そのまま残す内容を 1 文で書く" :sample "These recent messages contain the fine-grained operational details needed for immediate decision-making: exact file contents read in the last few turns, specific error messages, precise line numbers, and the outcome of the most recent tool calls.")
(defrule dual-memory-working/a2 -> :instruction "要約しない理由を 1 文で書く" :sample "Summarization would destroy exactly the details that matter most for the next action.")
(defrule dual-memory-combined -> :nucleus dual-memory-combined/n :elaboration-additional dual-memory-combined/a1 :elaboration-additional dual-memory-combined/a2)
(defrule dual-memory-combined/n -> :instruction "考える呼び出しの前に組み立てる文脈を 1 文で書く" :sample "Before each thinking LLM call, the system constructs the thinking context by concatenating: (1) the episodic memory summary, providing the “big picture”; (2) the working memory messages, providing operational detail; and (3) the current user query.")
(defrule dual-memory-combined/a1 -> :instruction "この構造がなぞるものを 1 文で書く" :sample "This structure mirrors the distinction between episodic and working memory in cognitive architecture [8]: episodic memory stores the gist of past experience for long-range planning, while working memory holds detailed, recently acquired information for immediate use.")
(defrule dual-memory-combined/a2 -> :instruction "長さが有界である理由を 1 文で書く" :sample "The thinking token budget remains bounded regardless of conversation length, since the episodic summary has a fixed maximum length (500 characters) and the working memory window is constant.")
(defrule dual-memory-design-evolution -> :nucleus dual-memory-design-evolution/n :elaboration-additional dual-memory-design-evolution/a1 :elaboration-additional dual-memory-design-evolution/a2 :elaboration-additional dual-memory-design-evolution/a3)
(defrule dual-memory-design-evolution/n -> :instruction "要約だけを使った初期の試みと、その失敗を 1 文で書く" :sample "Early attempts used pure summarization for the entire history, but critical identifiers (file paths, variable names) were lost, causing the agent to reference non-existent files or misname functions.")
(defrule dual-memory-design-evolution/a1 -> :instruction "直近だけを使った場合の失敗を 1 文で書く" :sample "The opposite extreme, using only recent messages, lost long-range strategic context: the agent would “forget” the user’s original goal after 10 turns.")
(defrule dual-memory-design-evolution/a2 -> :instruction "混合方式が両方の失敗を解くことを 1 文で書く" :sample "The hybrid architecture addresses both failure modes.")
(defrule dual-memory-design-evolution/a3 -> :instruction "要約の要約が誤りを溜めることと、その対策を 1 文で書く" :sample "We also discovered that summarizing a previous summary (incremental summarization) accumulates errors over multiple rounds; periodic regeneration from the full history corrects this drift.")
